{"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Accessibility","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder is often the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" thing on screen for a few hundred milliseconds, or the only thing a user with a slow connection sees for much longer than that — so it’s worth it being as accessible as the real content it stands in for. The default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefault{Empty,Loading,Error}View"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":"s handle all of this out of the box; this article rounds up what they do and how a fully custom placeholder can match them."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"VoiceOver announcements","anchor":"VoiceOver-announcements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each default placeholder announces its own appearance — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_:).post()"},{"type":"text","text":" in SwiftUI, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.post(notification:.announcement, argument:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in UIKit — so a screen settling into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":" is heard, not just seen."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" exposes that same wording for any case, so a fully custom placeholder can announce transitions consistently instead of inventing its own text:"}]},{"code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full examples."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reduce Motion","anchor":"Reduce-Motion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Loading placeholder’s ring spins via a repeating rotation animation — purely decorative, and exactly the kind of large, continuous motion Reduce Motion exists to suppress. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityReduceMotion"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"},{"type":"text","text":" reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isReduceMotionEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" and also observes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.reduceMotionStatusDidChangeNotification"},{"type":"text","text":", so an already-visible spinner responds immediately if the setting changes while on screen, not just on the next appearance. Either way, the ring stays static — still colorful, just not spinning — instead of disabling itself entirely, since a static ring still communicates “loading” on its own."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Increase Contrast","anchor":"Increase-Contrast"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three default placeholders’ gradient icons\/ring respect Increase Contrast — SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorSchemeContrast"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value, UIKit’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isDarkerSystemColorsEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" (observed live the same way Reduce Motion is). A multi-stop gradient can dip below an acceptable contrast ratio in places a single flat color never does, so when Increase Contrast is on, every gradient is swapped for a solid "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".label"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primary"},{"type":"text","text":" tint instead."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dynamic Type","anchor":"Dynamic-Type"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Error placeholders’ text scales with Dynamic Type: SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" get this for free from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContentUnavailableView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own text styles, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorUIView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s labels use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body, compatibleWith:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Both are covered up to the largest accessibility size by snapshot tests, so a regression that silently pins the text to a fixed size would be caught. The default Loading placeholder has no text at all — its ring is a fixed-size shape, unaffected by Dynamic Type by design."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Identifiers for XCUITest","anchor":"Identifiers-for-XCUITest"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder exposes a stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":", independent of any localized or custom text, so a UI test can assert which state is showing without string-matching:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Identifier","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shown on","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.loading"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.empty"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.retryButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Retry button, when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" is given","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.secondaryActionButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The secondary action button, when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secondaryAction"},{"text":" is given","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility"]}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateSt